{title: Favorite Song Of All}
{key: D}

{comment: Verse 1}
[D]He loves to hear the wind sing
As it [G]whistles through the pines on mountain [D]peaks.
[D]He loves to hear the raindrops
As they [G]splash to the ground in a magic melo[A]dy.
He [G]smiles in sweet approval
[G]As the waves crash to the rocks in harmo[Bm]ny.
Cr[G]eation joins in unity to sing to Him majestic sympho[A]nies.

{comment: Chorus}
{ci: NC}
But His favorite song of [G]all, is the song of the re[Bm]deemed,
[Bm]When lost sinners now made [A]clean,  lift their voices loud and [D]strong,
[D]When those purchased by His [G]blood,  lift to Him a song of [Bm]love,
[Bm]Nothing more He'd rather [A]hear, nor so pleasing to His ear,
[A]As His favorite song of [D]all.

{comment: Verse 2}
[D]He love to hear the angels as they [G]sing, "Holy, holy is the [D]Lamb"
[D](Holy holy, holy is the Lamb)
[D]Heaven's choirs in harmony [G]lift up praises to the great "I [A]AM"
[A](Alleluia, Alleluia)
But He [G]lifts His hands for silence when the weakest saved by grace
Begin to [Bm]sing.  (Ah Ah Ah)
And a [G]million angels listen as a newborn soul sing,
"I have been re[A]deemed"

{comment: Interlude}
[D]It's not just [G]melodies and harmonies that catches His attention
It's not just [Bm]clever lines and phrases that causes Him to stop and listen
But when [G]any heart set free, washed and bought by Calvary,
Begins to [A]sing.

{comment: Chorus Key Whole Step}
{ci: NC}
But His favorite song of [A]all, is the song of the re[E/Db]deemed,
When lost sinners now made [B]clean,  lift their voices loud and [E]strong,
When those purchased by His [A]blood,  lift to Him a song of [E/Db]love,[E]
Nothing more He'd rather [B]hear, nor so pleasing to His ear,
As His favorite song of [E]all.
[E]Halleluia, Holy is the Lamb.  Holy, holy
{ci: Repeat last line and fade out}
